r_feedback","digest":"9b1c206262782748998b2ff952f96f1a9ba6f03148d9e8c33e208c1c22e95657"}],"overlays":[],"round":0,"occurred_at":"2026-11-12T23:18:04.403Z","payload":{"actor":"founder","event":"plan.revision_requested","facts":{"gatewayOnline":true,"feedbackAttached":true},"scope":{"repo":"MADVenturesLLC/founder-os-build-room","paths":["docs/gateway-ops-actions-log-runbook.md"],"roomId":"eb4ccc7a-e014-48a8-a019-986f8fe7babe"},"eventId":"evt_6f4e80c2-e16f-4fb2-a3a0-671ad230971f","evidence":[{"ref":"cmd_planner_4cab80d3befa573a14da8c43f7e51e5a","kind":"plandoc","digest":"b45e69830d9073c51b4880f3af20782aca7028935273fe1edd50962ba98a8176"},{"ref":"evt_6f4e80c2-e16f-4fb2-a3a0-671ad230971f","kind":"founder_feedback","digest":"9b1c206262782748998b2ff952f96f1a9ba6f03148d9e8c33e208c1c22e95657"}],"feedback":"Revise. Checked against the checkout at 6b80c2259558e93d4f12dca474cc1d491930bd5d, these statements are false. Correct each as stated here, or remove it, and keep the rest as it is.\n1. current_state says docs/gateway-ops-actions-log-runbook.md contains six sections, then lists seven. It has seven \"## \" sections, with headings at lines 12, 31, 48, 69, 100, 141 and 149.\n2. Constraint 5 cites AGENTS.md line 40 for the rule against creating or modifying governance doctrine. Line 40 is blank; the rule is at line 35.\n3. No refusal code staging_lock_busy exists anywhere in the repository. When the staging lock is held, runEnroll returns the code of StagingLockBusy, which is staging_busy_or_recovery_required (packages/gateway-daemon/src/staging-lock.ts line 50; packages/gateway-cli/src/enroll.ts lines 68-79). Use that code everywhere the plan names staging_lock_busy.\n4. buildroom doctor prints only renderDoctor's text (packages/gateway-cli/src/bin.ts line 147). That text has no stopCondition line and does not show field names such as daemon.reachable, daemon.reason or socketPath. For an orphaned lock it prints \"present: yes\", then \"pid: N (not live)\" when the lock's metadata can be read, then the guidance line that begins \"orphaned staging lock: this is a fail-closed stop condition\" (packages/gateway-cli/src/doctor.ts lines 121-125 and 145-156). For the daemon it prints \"reachable: no (reason)\" and \"socket: path\" (lines 136-138). Describe what doctor prints, not the report's field names.\n5. observability says gateway_enrollment_refusals is written whenever redeem or a Founder act is refused. On the Founder routes only the 409 refusals write a row there (store.ts lines 247-253, 258-264, 275-281, 296-302, 349-352, 390-396, 407-413); a 400, 401, 404 or 413 on those routes writes nothing to either table. POST /gateway/enroll records its 400 validation refusals (routes.ts lines 112-123) and its 409 refusals (store.ts lines 515-614). Say that, and where the plan has the reader inspect gateway_enrollment_refusals after a 400, limit it to POST /gateway/enroll.\n6. data_flow says the Founder act flow emits an operational log line named founder_act, and observability lists founder_act log lines. No code in the repository emits a log line of that name; its only mention is docs/gateway-ops-actions-log-runbook.md line 23. Remove both claims, and do not send the reader to that log line.\n7. known_risks gives a path with a :line suffix inside the backticks as an example of a span that fails scripts/path-audit.sh. The audit's pattern (line 82) allows no colon, so such a span does not match and is skipped, not checked. Remove the example.\n8. error_and_failure_behavior and trust_and_security_boundaries attribute recording the gateway.enrollment_denied row to B5. B5 (line 17) says only to deny the enrollment and stop. The row for a deliberate deny comes from docs/gateway-ops-actions-log-runbook.md lines 41-42; cite the runbook for it.\nChange nothing the feedback does not name; copy every hash and path from the earlier plan exactly.\nBefore returning the plan, check every name, line number and claim about behaviour against the files you read, and remove any you did not see.","occurredAt":"2026-11-12T23:18:04.403Z","attribution":{"roleId":null,"actorId":"founder","actualModel":"n/a (human Founder decision)","executionSurface":"founder-terminal"}},"committed_at":"2026-11-12T23:18:04.381Z"},{"seq":"5","event_id":"evt_5a88dc66-277b-4b1d-a06a-e3d15b835a71","event":"plan.submitted","outcome":"transition","entry_seq":5,"transition_id":"T3","guard_id":"G3","from_state":"PLANNING","resulting_state":"PLAN_REVIEW","actor":"agent.planner","attribution":{"roleId":"architect","actorId":"gateway:1880c12d-d98d-4a91-b25a-23320aa7f58a","actualModel":"gemini-4-argon","executionSurface":"antigravity"},"scope":{"repo":"MADVenturesLLC/founder-os-build-room","paths":["docs/gateway-ops-actions-log-runbook.md"],"roomId":"eb4ccc7a-e014-48a8-a019-986f8fe7babe"},"evidence":[{"ref":"cmd_planner_3232ea81e79e24d0b0cabde7cfc3f796","kind":"plandoc","digest":"427217b4c338b838d6b9649fa4211b42babff3c69e2cdc27806e3288b9ced0d0"}],"overlays":[],"round":0,"occurred_at":"2026-11-12T23:22:10.513Z","payload":{"actor":"agent.planner","event":"plan.submitted","facts":{"planHash":"427217b4c338b838d6b9649fa4211b42babff3c69e2cdc27806e3288b9ced0d0","gatewayOnline":true,"planDocSchemaValid":true},"scope":{"repo":"MADVenturesLLC/founder-os-build-room","paths":["docs/gateway-ops-actions-log-runbook.md"],"roomId":"eb4ccc7a-e014-48a8-a019-986f8fe7babe"},"eventId":"evt_5a88dc66-277b-4b1d-a06a-e3d15b835a71","evidence":[{"ref":"cmd_planner_3232ea81e79e24d0b0cabde7cfc3f796","kind":"plandoc","digest":"427217b4c338b838d6b9649fa4211b42babff3c69e2cdc27806e3288b9ced0d0"}],"occurredAt":"2026-11-12T23:22:10.513Z","attribution":{"roleId":"architect","actorId":"gateway:1880c12d-d98d-4a91-b25a-23320aa7f58a","actualModel":"gemini-4-argon","executionSurface":"antigravity"}},"committed_at":"2026-11-12T23:22:10.496Z"},{"seq":"6","event_id":"evt_f5e756fb-8ba2-48dc-9fa8-5b1b54e37661","event":"plan.approved","outcome":"transition","entry_seq":6,"transition_id":"T5","guard_id":"G